{"id":"736f8cdd-bf0c-44c3-9168-89624cb0734c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1aea7f344fb0ee03","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/cspell/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"754d55ed3592b5766e5e85a22f9760ed94e9f177","start":1213,"end":1331},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","worker","=","new","Worker","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","joinPath","(","context",".","extensionUri",",","\"","server.js","\"",")",".","toString","(","true",")",",","{","\"","name","\"",":","\"","cspell","\"","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"9e92e4af3727b748","after":"41fda70fb0267fa5"}},"payload":{"text":"server.js is a classic bootstrap that imports the module worker (an extension's workers start classic).\n(named, so the architecture view and the memory gauge call it cspell)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:15.682Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:15.682Z"}
{"id":"c8935157-8a4f-4176-b313-76e9db1b73ef","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"15dff974c2835664","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/cspell/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6f21a48185caecc1a6880f6726e7b0071ccb28cf","start":632,"end":813},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","DOCUMENTS","=","[","\"","typescript","\"",",","\"","typescriptreact","\"",",","\"","javascript","\"",",","\"","javascriptreact","\"",",","\"","plaintext","\"",",","\"","markdown","\"",",","\"","json","\"","]",".","map","(","(","language",")","=>","(","{","\"","language","\"",":","language",",","\"","scheme","\"",":","\"","file","\"","}",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"cff9941f13daaab1","after":"3d0d20c9710798d1"}},"payload":{"text":"The documents it checks: the workspace's files, by language — not a diff's other side (`git-head:`, a commit's), which is\nthe same words again. The react language ids matter: a .tsx file's languageId is `typescriptreact`, and a client only\nforwards documents its selector names.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:15.942Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:15.942Z"}
{"id":"cb14ab5e-b335-4066-9aaa-c7b6fafdd795","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ef525116119cff33","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/cspell/extension.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cadcdfab1449b007de2547c3d32c68391fb48b7b","start":0,"end":78},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","failureText",",","watchWorker","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/failures","\""]},"context":{"after":"f2517b5f32f25ee8"}},"payload":{"text":"cspell — spell-checks code and prose with the real cspell engine, a Node program, run in a worker of this extension's\nown under almostnode (server-host.ts runs server-node.ts there) and connected to the editor as an ordinary language\nserver with a vscode-languageclient. Public API only: the worker reads nothing of the workspace (documents come over\nLSP; its dictionary is its own), so nothing the editor's core has is needed here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:16.231Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:27:16.231Z"}
